    "text": "Two uniformly charged nonconducting spheres, each of radius&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>, are fixed in a gravity free space as shown in the figure. If an electron is released at rest from the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>,&nbsp;then its speed just before striking the other sphere is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo></math>mass of electron =&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></math><br />\r<br />\r<br />\r&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/0007273__solution_.PNG\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 104px;\" />",
